# Forest boss (Boss, 2026-11-21): native 48x32 frames, facing right, feet on row 31. A horned warlord in blackened iron
# (i/I/J) under a mulberry tabard and cape (p/P with magenta lights M), bone horns h and two ember eyes e in the visor, with a
# long-hafted bearded axe: a crescent edge S with a lit bevel B on steel s, a beard hooking down from the iron eye `j`
# where the ash haft w passes through, and a back spike. The axe's own ink `a` and eye `j` share the colours of the ink k and
# the iron J; they are separate characters, like the bevel B, so tests/test_enemy_sprites.py can tell the weapon from the body.
# Boxes (Boss.java, unchanged): the body x 8..23, y 5..31 of every live frame, a pixel inside the body hitbox rect(7, 4, 18, 28)
# (D10); the axe is drawn into NORMAL_BOX rect(24, 22, 16, 8) on the sweep (x 24..39, y 22..29, edge to edge) and into
# COUNTER_BOX rect(24, 12, 16, 15) on both counter frames (x 24..39, y 12..26), and outside the hitbox on no other frame
# that hurts. Exported by tools/enemy_sprites.py into assets/images/enemy/Boss.png in the cells Boss.java reads
# (sprite_layouts.ENEMY_SHEETS).
# idle1..4: standing, the axe upright in the back fist, breathing and the cape stirring (IDLE and RECOVERY); walk1..4: stride,
# pass, stride, pass. The two attacks read apart. The normal attack is low and level: raise, cock (the axe drawn back to the
# hip, then down behind the heel in a crouch, the eyes staying red), sweep (the head swung level at the knees, dashed trail),
# follow (the blade bitten into the ground). The counter is high and overhead: warn1, warn2 (the axe straight up over the
# horns, then hanging down his back, the eyes white; the game tints them orange), counter1 (the chop starting, the fists thrown
# up over the helm and the haft coming down over his head into the box, its trail falling ahead of the blade), counter2 (the chop landed, the haft slanting down from raised fists; held through
# COUNTER_RECOVERY). recoil, flash: the hurt reaction; throne1..4: the rest state, sitting on the ground with one knee up, the
# axe standing beside him, the eyes smouldering; stagger, kneel, fall, ash: the death (the eyes dimming to M), ending as ash.
# Danger family, its own hue: the mulberry 6e1460 (OKLab hue -25) and magenta b03a8c lie off the beetle's crimson 86101f,
# the bugs' rose 9c2050, the red mob's wine 6c0014 and scarlet f80440 (each at least 0.077 away); no skin, so the hero's
# copper and tan stay his own. The moon rim (D92) lights the ink contour on export.
